# file-mcp-server Docker Deployment Guide

This runbook is for deployment agents building and operating `file-mcp-server` in containers with local, S3, WebDAV, FTP, and Google Drive backends.

## 1. Build image

```bash
./docker-build.sh cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

Direct build:

```bash
docker buildx build --load --network=host -t cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest .
```

Build with enterprise CA/proxy:

```bash
CUSTOM_CA_CERT=/path/to/enterprise-ca.crt \
HTTP_PROXY=http://proxy.local:3128 \
HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.local:3128 \
./docker-build.sh cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

## 2. Persistent host layout

Recommended host directories:

```text
/srv/file-mcp/
  workspace/      # scope root and local backend data
  logs/           # server.log, audit.log.jsonl, snapshots/
  certs/          # trusted CA bundle(s)
  env/
    base.env
    backend.local.env
    backend.webdav.env
    backend.ftp.env
    backend.s3.env
    backend.gdrive.env
```

Local test layout in repo:

```bash
mkdir -p run/workspace run/logs certs
cp docker-env.example run/env.base
```

## 3. Default initial configuration (single env)

Minimal bootstrap env:

```bash
cat > run/env.base <<'ENV'
FILE_MCP_API_KEY_PRIMARY=change-me
FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=local
FILE_MCP_ROOT=/workspace
FILE_MCP_AUDIT_LOG=/workspace/logs/audit.log.jsonl
FILE_MCP_SERVER_LOG=/workspace/logs/server.log
FILE_MCP_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/workspace/logs/snapshots
FILE_MCP_HTTP_TRANSPORT=streamable-http
FILE_MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
FILE_MCP_HTTP_PORT=8000
ENV
```

Run:

```bash
docker run --rm --name file-mcp-server \
  --network=host \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/workspace:/workspace" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/logs:/workspace/logs" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/env.base:/workspace/env.base:ro" \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.base \
  -e FILE_MCP_CONFIG_PATH=/app/config.yaml \
  -e FILE_MCP_DEFAULTS_PATH=/app/defaults.yaml \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

Validate:

```bash
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
```

## 4. Multi-configuration support

### 4.1 Layered env files

The runtime supports comma-separated env files in `FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH`.

```bash
docker run --rm --name file-mcp-server \
  --network=host \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/workspace:/workspace" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/logs:/workspace/logs" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/env.base:/workspace/env.base:ro" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/env.override:/workspace/env.override:ro" \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.base,/workspace/env.override \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

Precedence:
1. OS environment (`docker run -e ...`)
2. Env file list (`FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=file1,file2`)
3. `config.yaml`
4. `defaults.yaml`

### 4.2 Multiple profiles in config.yaml

Define profile-specific backends in mounted `config.yaml`, then select with `FILE_MCP_PROFILE`:

```bash
-e FILE_MCP_CONFIG_PATH=/workspace/config.yaml \
-e FILE_MCP_PROFILE=prod-s3
```

Optional hot reload endpoint after config update:
- `POST /admin/reload`

### 4.3 Required changes for one-container, four-profile deployment

Deployment agent checklist:
1. Use a mounted multi-profile config file:
   - `docker-config.profiles.example.yaml` -> `/srv/file-mcp/config.yaml`
2. Provide one API key per profile in env:
   - `FILE_MCP_API_KEY_LOCAL`
   - `FILE_MCP_API_KEY_S3`
   - `FILE_MCP_API_KEY_WEBDAV`
   - `FILE_MCP_API_KEY_FTP`
3. Provide endpoint credentials in env:
   - S3: `FILE_MCP_S3_ENDPOINT`, `FILE_MCP_S3_BUCKET`, `FILE_MCP_S3_ACCESS_KEY`, `FILE_MCP_S3_SECRET_KEY`
   - WebDAV: `FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_BASE_URL`, `FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_USERNAME`, `FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_PASSWORD`
   - FTP: `FILE_MCP_FTP_HOST`, `FILE_MCP_FTP_USERNAME`, `FILE_MCP_FTP_PASSWORD`
4. Set server default profile:
   - `FILE_MCP_PROFILE=local` (recommended default)
5. Mount config and env into container and set:
   - `FILE_MCP_CONFIG_PATH=/workspace/config.yaml`
   - `FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.base`

Example run (all 4 profiles active in one process):

```bash
docker run -d --name file-mcp-server \
  --network=host \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/workspace:/workspace \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/logs:/workspace/logs \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/certs:/app/certs:ro \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/env/base.env:/workspace/env.base:ro \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/config.yaml:/workspace/config.yaml:ro \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.base \
  -e FILE_MCP_CONFIG_PATH=/workspace/config.yaml \
  -e FILE_MCP_PROFILE=local \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

Profile selection at runtime:
- default/fallback profile: `FILE_MCP_PROFILE`
- query selector: `POST /mcp?profile=s3`
- header selector: `X-File-MCP-Profile: webdav`
- each selected profile requires its own API key.

## 5. Certificates and TLS behavior

Mount certs and trust bundle:

```bash
docker run --rm --name file-mcp-server \
  --network=host \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/workspace:/workspace" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/logs:/workspace/logs" \
  -v "$(pwd)/certs:/app/certs:ro" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/env.base:/workspace/env.base:ro" \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.base \
  -e FILE_MCP_STORAGE_TLS_CA_BUNDLE=/app/certs/ca.crt \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

Disable remote-backend TLS verification (explicit risk opt-in):

```bash
-e FILE_MCP_STORAGE_TLS_INSECURE=true
```

## 6. Backend-specific env examples

Use one backend per running profile/env.

### 6.1 Local

```bash
FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=local
FILE_MCP_ROOT=/workspace
```

### 6.2 WebDAV

```bash
FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=webdav
FILE_MCP_ROOT=/
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_BASE_URL=https://files.example.com/remote.php/dav/files/user/root
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_USERNAME=user
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_PASSWORD=secret
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_MOVE_RETRY_COUNT=2
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_MOVE_RETRY_BACKOFF_S=0.35
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_MOVE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_S=5
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_MOVE_RETRY_STATUSES=408,409,423,425,429,500,502,503,504
```

### 6.3 FTP

```bash
FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=ftp
FILE_MCP_ROOT=/
FILE_MCP_FTP_HOST=ftp.example.com
FILE_MCP_FTP_PORT=21
FILE_MCP_FTP_USERNAME=user
FILE_MCP_FTP_PASSWORD=secret
FILE_MCP_FTP_BASE_DIR=/
FILE_MCP_FTP_USE_TLS=false
```

### 6.4 S3

```bash
FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=s3
FILE_MCP_ROOT=/
FILE_MCP_S3_ENDPOINT=https://storage.example.com
FILE_MCP_S3_BUCKET=my-bucket
FILE_MCP_S3_REGION=us-east-1
FILE_MCP_S3_ACCESS_KEY=...
FILE_MCP_S3_SECRET_KEY=...
FILE_MCP_S3_PREFIX=
```

### 6.5 Google Drive

```bash
FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=google_drive
FILE_MCP_ROOT=/
FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_FOLDER_ID=1r6kwtGcunVpkbT3nBGmfcWyVfk84_Sjn
FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_CLIENT_ID=...
FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=...
FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_REFRESH_TOKEN=...
FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_TOKEN_URI=https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token
```

## 7. Standard run command (any backend)

```bash
docker run --rm --name file-mcp-server \
  --network=host \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/workspace:/workspace \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/logs:/workspace/logs \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/certs:/app/certs:ro \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/env/backend.s3.env:/workspace/env.base:ro \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.base \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

## 8. Optional admin UI and Google OAuth

Enable:

```bash
FILE_MCP_ADMIN_UI_ENABLED=true
FILE_MCP_ADMIN_UI_TOKEN=change-me
FILE_MCP_ADMIN_APPLY_ON_CALLBACK=true
```

Endpoints:
- `GET /admin/google-drive`
- `POST /admin/google-drive/start`
- `GET /admin/google-drive/callback`
- `POST /admin/reload`

## 9. HTTP/API endpoints for deployment

- `GET /` (status summary; browser HTML or JSON with `Accept: application/json`)
- `GET /health`
- `POST /mcp`
- `GET /admin/google-drive` (if admin UI enabled)
- `POST /admin/google-drive/start` (if admin UI enabled)
- `GET /admin/google-drive/callback` (if admin UI enabled)
- `POST /admin/reload` (if admin UI enabled)

Authoritative machine-readable spec: `openapi.json`

Per-request profile override on `/mcp`:
- query: `?profile=<profile-name>`
- header: `X-File-MCP-Profile: <profile-name>`
- fallback: server default profile (`FILE_MCP_PROFILE`)

## 10. Container management

Foreground:

```bash
docker run --rm ... cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

Detached + inspect logs:

```bash
docker run -d --name file-mcp-server ... cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
docker logs -f file-mcp-server
```

